codex
I found one possible rescue and am checking it before finalizing the rejection: the paper’s six-fiber Hopf representation plus its global phase invariance may support a native Track B selection problem with many exact phase decoys, fixed 24-point output, and a large generic-CSP/short-common-phase gap. I’ll only replace the rejection if the exact geometry and the adversary requirements both hold.
