Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s six-fiber Hopf representation of the 24-cell and common-phase symmetry ([paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.4884)).

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4884/gen_1301_4884.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4884/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4884/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4884/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4884/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1301.4884/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local gates pass:

- G1: 12/12 deterministic planted witnesses verify.
- G4: 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses succeeded.
- G5: exactly 1/46,656 valid easy answers; reference CSP solves 8/8 shipping instances with median 64,876 exact operations.
- G6: four no-tool attacks each failed 0/8.
- G8: 20/20 symmetry invariance tests and 20/20 unrelated-key distinctions.
- G9(c): 387 characters, 48 atomic elements, 192 intended arithmetic operations.

The required external hardness evidence remains incomplete: all bare, hinted, and placebo OpenRouter calls returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” The transcripts record those provider errors, but they are not evidence that the family defeated the oracle pool. After replenishing the key, rerun the three hardening arms before submission.
