-```
-
-## Caveats
-
-- The hardness claim is **not trusted until the bare four-vendor loop holds a rung**.
-  The current local results establish construction and exact verification only.
-- `P(guess)=0/200,000` uses the declared prior: one uniformly random listed orbit per
-  fiber. It does not measure a solver that recognizes common Hopf phase or runs CSP.
-- The full Gram-value multiset is invariant under candidate order, fiber relabeling,
-  quarter-turn representative changes, and global orthogonal phase. It is a strong
-  cheap invariant, not a complete isometry canonical form; rare cospectral collisions
-  could over-collapse instances.
-- The exact compatibility CSP was tested, but no SDP relaxation or general-purpose
-  SMT solver was run. For this rigid six-fiber construction, the exact CSP is the more
-  direct domain-standard baseline.
-- A propagated restart over every starting orbit succeeds and is part of the disclosed
-  reference algorithm. The failing 256-restart probe samples complete answers without
-  that exact geometric propagation.
-- Increasing beyond 21 candidates per fiber would push the intended phase-normalizing
-  route above the 300-operation no-tool cap. `escalate()` therefore has only one rung
-  beyond the named ladder.
+The built module is retained as `rejected_gen_1301_4884.py`; the script-owned
+oracle evidence is `llm_loop_transcript.jsonl` with metadata in `.meta.json`.
+The paper itself is [Delimiting Maximal Kissing Configurations in Four
+Dimensions](https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.4884).
